#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:1
msgid "Gazebo Release Instructions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:3
msgid "Initial setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:5
msgid ""
"A small number of configurations and credentials need to be made on the "
"developer's system before triggering the release.  If a permanent operating "
"system is used for releasing, these installation steps only need to be "
"executed once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:10
msgid "1. Software and configurations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:12
msgid ""
"Triggering the releasing process is only supported on Linux at this moment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:14
msgid ""
"The tool designed to facilitate the process of releasing software for all "
"platforms is called [`release.py`](https://github.com/gazebo-tooling/release-"
"tools/blob/master/release.py), and is hosted at https://github.com/gazebo-"
"tooling/release-tools. Cloning the `release-tools` repository is required to "
"perform a new release:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:18
msgid ""
"cd ~/\n"
"git clone https://github.com/gazebo-tooling/release-tools.git\n"
msgstr ""
"cd ~/\n"
"git clone https://github.com/gazebo-tooling/release-tools.git\n"

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:23
msgid "Some Debian tools require the following variables to be set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:24
msgid ""
"export DEBEMAIL=\"<username>@openrobotics.org\"\n"
"export DEBFULLNAME=\"<Your full name>\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:29
msgid ""
"**Note:** the two above exported variables can be added to `.bashrc` to have "
"them configured automatically on every run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:32
msgid "2. Access and Credentials"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:34
msgid ""
"Before starting the release process, make sure to ask for write access to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:35
msgid "The Gz library intended to be released and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:36
msgid "`gazebo-release` repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:38
msgid ""
"To interact with Jenkins an API token needs to be created and stored in the "
"user system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:41
msgid ""
"Creating a Jenkins API token: Open [https://build.osrfoundation.org/user/"
"<user\\>/security/](https://build.osrfoundation.org/user/<user>/security/) "
"(Remember to change `<user>` to your username). In the \"API Token\" "
"section, there is an `Add new Token` button to add a new Jenkins API token."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:47
msgid "The token needs to be stored in `~/.buildfarm/jenkins.ini` in the form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:48
msgid ""
"[https://build.osrfoundation.org]\n"
"username = <your-github-user>\n"
"password = <token created in step 1>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:54
msgid "For Each Release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:56
msgid "1. Team and development checks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:58
msgid ""
"When creating a new release, there are some guidelines to follow before "
"starting the process:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:61
msgid "Ask the team if there are any concerns about making the release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:62
msgid ""
"Check if there are changes to previous library versions that need to be "
"forward-ported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:63
msgid ""
"See if there are open PRs against the release branch (release branch is the "
"one with the name `ign/gz-fooX` where foo is the name of the Gz library and "
"X the major version of the version bump planned) that could go into the new "
"release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:68
msgid "2. Update code version and changelogs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:70
msgid ""
"The first step to get a new release ready is to update the current code "
"(upstream) version (view the [versioning](release.md#versioning) section for "
"more information). This bump could be in the major number (non-compatible "
"changes), minor number (new features), patch number (patches and bugfixes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:75
msgid ""
"**Bumping major number** of the version implies some work to have the "
"metadata updated correctly. There is a [dedicated document](releasing/"
"bump_major.md) that you should go through before continuing to work through "
"the steps in this document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:80
msgid ""
"To update the upstream version a local checkout of the Gz library is needed. "
"A new branch is required to submit changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:83
msgid ""
"# version X.Y.Z\n"
"git checkout -b bump_to_X_Y_Z\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:88
msgid ""
"The current upstream version can be found in `CMakeLists.txt` file following "
"the CMake `project declaration`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:91
msgid ""
"# Gz library named foo and version X.Y.Z\n"
"project(gz-fooX VERSION X.Y.Z)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:96
msgid ""
"Stable releases can modify the X, Y or Z directly while prereleases will "
"need to include the preX (X number starts with 1) suffix in the "
"`gz_configure_project`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:98
msgid ""
"# first prerelease of a series, number 1\n"
"gz_configure_project(VERSION_SUFFIX pre1)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:103
msgid ""
"Together with bumping the version number, **updating the Changelog and "
"Migration documents** is required. For updating the `Changelog.md` file, the "
"script [source_changelog.bash](https://github.com/gazebo-tooling/release-"
"tools/blob/master/source-repo-scripts/source_changelog.bash) can be useful:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:108
msgid ""
"cd <path to source code>\n"
"bash <path to release-tools>/source-repo-scripts/source_changelog.bash "
"<previous tag>\n"
"# e.g. bash ../release-tools/source-repo-scripts/source_changelog.bash "
"3.5.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:113
msgid ""
"The `Migration.md` document needs to be updated if some breaking changes are "
"in the Changelog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:115
msgid ""
"Open a pull request for reviewing ([example PR](https://github.com/gazebosim/"
"gz-physics/pull/447)). When opening a PR look for the \"Release\" section in "
"the template and follow the instructions there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:118
msgid "3. Update packages version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:120
msgid ""
"Once the PR for bumping the code version is merged, the binary packages "
"version needs to be updated for the Debian/Ubuntu packages. Brew metadata "
"will be updated by the building server when creating the binary packages "
"(known as `bottles`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:125
msgid ""
"The version in the packages (binary version) should be similar to the one "
"updated in the code in the step above but usually has some other components "
"that reflect the package metadata version (i.e: new code version 2.1.0, new "
"version in Debian packages is usually 2.1.0-1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:130
msgid ""
"There should be a repository matching the name and major version of Gz "
"library that you want to bump in the [gz-release](https://github.com/gazebo-"
"release/) GitHub organization. (see [release repositories document]"
"(releasing/release_repositories.md) for more information about how they are "
"used)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:136
msgid ""
"It is required to clone the corresponding release repository to update the "
"binary version:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:139
msgid ""
"# Gz library named foo and major version X\n"
"git clone https://github.com/gazebo-release/gz-fooX-release\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:144
msgid ""
"To bump the package versions that will appear in Debian/Ubuntu binary "
"packages there is a helper script in `release-tools` (see [initial setup]"
"(#initial-setup)). The script is called `changelog_spawn.sh` and require to "
"be executed while the active directory is a `release repository`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:146
msgid ""
"# Gz library named foo and major version X\n"
"cd gz-fooX-release\n"
"~/release-tools/release-repo-scripts/changelog_spawn.sh X.Y.Z-R\n"
"\n"
"# Example gz-cmake3 bumped from 3.0.0 to 3.0.1\n"
"cd gz-cmake3-release\n"
"~/release-tools/release-repo-scripts/changelog_spawn.sh 3.0.1-1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:156
msgid ""
"`changelog_spawn.sh` will display information about the Ubuntu/Debian "
"versions being updated as well as a `git diff` before uploading information "
"to the GitHub release repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:158
msgid "Triggering the release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:160
msgid ""
"After updating the code and releasing metadata everything is ready to launch "
"the build in the server. Now, the following needs to happen:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:163
msgid ""
"Tag the corresponding code in the repository and upload that tag to GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:164
msgid ""
"Request `build.osrfoundation.org` server to start a chain of job by calling "
"`gz-fooX-source`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:165
msgid ""
"`gz-fooX-source` will generate the source tarball and call "
"`repository_uploader_packages` to upload it to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:166
msgid ""
"`gz-fooX-source` will call `_releasepy` that will generate the builders jobs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:167
msgid "Debian/Ubuntu: use `ign/gz-fooX-debbuilder` job names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:168
msgid "Brew: entry job is `generic-release-homebrew_pull_request_updater`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:170
msgid ""
"The `release.py` script  and Jenkins will perform all these actions. For "
"more information of all the processes triggered by the `release.py` script "
"please check [the release process](release.md#using-the-gzdev-repository-"
"command)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:173
msgid "4. Executing release.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:175
msgid ""
"Make sure you are in the source code repository before running `release.py`. "
"You should be on the branch to be released, after the pull request bumping "
"the version has been merged (run `git status` to check the branch, and "
"`git     log` to check that the version bump pull request has been "
"included). Running `release.py` from the source code repository will "
"generate and upload some Git tags (\"release tags\") to the source code "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:182
msgid ""
"You will also need the token described in the [credentials section](#2-"
"access-and-credentials)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:185
msgid ""
"There are a few external dependencies for running release.py. They can be "
"easily installed using virtual environments and pip:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:188
msgid ""
"# you can change .releasepy_venv by any directory of your preference\n"
"python3 -m venv ~/.releasepy_venv\n"
". ~/.releasepy_venv/bin/activate\n"
"cd <release-tools-dir>\n"
"pip install .\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:196
msgid "**dry-run simulation mode**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:198
msgid ""
"The `release.py` tool supports a `--dry-run` flag that allows users to "
"simulate releases (nothing is modified) in order to ensure that the correct "
"arguments are being used to trigger a particular release.  Gz releasers "
"should **always** call `release.py` with `--dry-run` first in order to "
"ensure that proper commands are being used to trigger releases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:204
msgid ""
"The script needs to be run from the repository with the source code (i.e., "
"the repository where the Gz library version bump pull request took place):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:206
msgid ""
"# Example of dry-run for gz-cmake3 bumped to 3.0.1\n"
"cd gz-cmake3\n"
"git checkout gz-cmake3\n"
"~/release-tools/release.py gz-cmake3 3.0.1 --dry-run\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:213
msgid "**release.py for stable releases**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:215
msgid ""
"# Gz library named foo and major version X\n"
"cd ign/gz-fooX\n"
"git checkout ign/gz-fooX\n"
"\n"
"# Example gz-cmake3 bumped to 3.0.1\n"
"cd gz-cmake3\n"
"git checkout gz-cmake3\n"
"~/release-tools/release.py gz-cmake3 3.0.1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:226
msgid "**release.py for prereleases or nightlies**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:228
msgid ""
"When releasing prereleases or nightly releases, there are some special flags "
"to be set. The `--upload-to-repo` argument is mandatory when running "
"`release.py`, and should be set to `prerelease` or `nightly`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:232
msgid ""
"# Example gz-cmake3 bumped to prerelease 3.0.0~pre1\n"
"cd gz-cmake3\n"
"git checkout gz-cmake3\n"
"~/release-tools/release.py gz-cmake3 3.0.0~pre1 --upload-to-repo prerelease\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:239
msgid ""
"Nightly invocation is generally coded in the server. The version will be "
"taken from the last changelog entry and modified during building. No source "
"code will be uploaded, but taken directly in the binary build from the "
"branch pointed by `--nightly-src-branch`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:244
msgid ""
"# Example gz-cmake3 nightly from main branch\n"
"~/release-tools/release.py gz-cmake3 3.0.0~pre1 --upload-to-repo nightly --"
"nightly-src-branch main\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:249
msgid "**Binary version schema for prereleases and nightlies**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:251
msgid ""
"Prerelease and nightlies binary versions use particular naming schema to "
"define right ordering for package managers. [This information about "
"versioning](https://classic.gazebosim.org/tutorials?"
"tut=install_unstable&cat=install#Versioninginnightlyandprerelease) in Gazebo "
"Classic applies to the [Gazebo] too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:254
msgid "**release.py for revision bumps**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:256
msgid ""
"Bumping the [revision number for binary packages](release.md#versioning) is "
"a special case of releasing since the original tarball with the source code "
"will remain the same. Once the release repository is ready with the new "
"release version, `release.py` needs the `--only-bump-revision-linux` flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:261
msgid ""
"Note that the `--source-tarball-uri` parameter is needed with the original "
"tarball of the software version. All the tarballs can be found at https://"
"classic.gazebosim.org/distributions or the information should appear in the "
"parameters of the Jenkins -debbuilder build that created the first version "
"of the software."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:266
msgid ""
"# Example gz-cmake3 bumped from 3.0.1-1 to 3.0.1-2\n"
"~/release-tools/release.py gz-cmake3 3.0.1 --source-tarball-uri https://osrf-"
"distributions.s3.amazonaws.com/gz-cmake/releases/gz-cmake-3.0.1.tar.bz2 --"
"only-bump-revision-linux -release-version 2\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:271
msgid "Checking the Building Process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:273
msgid "For checking that the build process is ongoing as expected:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:275
msgid "Checking the source generation and upload:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:276
msgid ""
"The `gz-fooX-source` job (change fooX by the software name being released, i."
"e: math7) is triggered directly by `release.py` (script output will point to "
"it) should have finished successfully."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:278
msgid ""
"The `gz-fooX-source` job launches a one new build in the "
"`repository_uploader_packages` job with the name of the software."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:279
msgid "If there is a failure, contact with the Infra team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:280
msgid ""
"There should be one new build in the `_releasepy` job with the name of the "
"software."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:281
msgid ""
"If there is a failure, you can check the output if you can access to the job "
"workspace in the Jenkins build, since it is disabled by default. Contact "
"with the Infra team for help."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:283
msgid "Checking package generation after the `_releasepy` build:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:284
msgid ""
"Several `-debbuilder` jobs should be in https://build.osrfoundation.org/. "
"For watching the jobs to see if any of them fail or are marked unstable, "
"open the page for a specific debbuild, such as https://build.osrfoundation."
"org/job/gz-math7-debbuilder/."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:289
msgid ""
"If there is a failure, check the list of supported architectures in the "
"corresponding [Gazebo Platform Support issue](https://github.com/gazebo-"
"tooling/release-tools/issues?q=label%3A%22Tier+Platform+Support%22+)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:292
msgid ""
"To check if a debbuild has previously succeeded for a given architecture, "
"check packages.osrfoundation.org to see the most recent successful builds. "
"(i.e most recent [Ubuntu builds of ignition-gazebo6](https://packages."
"osrfoundation.org/gazebo/ubuntu-stable/pool/main/i/ignition-gazebo6/) or the "
"[Debian builds of ignition-gazebo6](https://packages.osrfoundation.org/"
"gazebo/debian-stable/pool/main/i/ignition-gazebo6/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:297
msgid ""
"If the failure is on a supported architecture, check the source repository "
"for an existing report of this failure and if none exists, report the "
"failure (see [gazebosim/gz-math#161](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-math/"
"issues/161) for an example)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:301
msgid ""
"If a build is unstable, check if it was unstable before this release and if "
"it has already been reported. A common cause of unstable debbuilds is newly "
"installed files that are not captured by the patterns in the `.install` "
"files in the `-release` repository. This can be checked by searching for "
"`dh_missing` in the console log of the unstable build and looking for a list "
"of uninstalled files. Example pull requests that fix problems with "
"`dh_missing` are [gazebo-release/gz-transport11-release#4](https://github."
"com/gazebo-release/gz-transport11-release/pull/4) and [gazebo-release/gz-"
"tools-release#4](https://github.com/gazebo-release/gz-tools-release/pull/4)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:308
msgid ""
"A pull request was opened to https://github.com/osrf/homebrew-simulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:309
msgid "This pull request may take a minute or two to open."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:310
msgid ""
"Once it is open, make a comment containing the text \"build bottle\". For "
"further details, see the [README at osrf/homebrew-simulation](https://github."
"com/osrf/homebrew-simulation#to-build-bottles)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:313
msgid ""
"A pull request was opened to  <https://github.com/gazebo-release/"
"$VENDOR_PACKAGE/>, where  `$VENDOR_PACKAGE` is the name of the Gazebo vendor "
"package for ROS (see  <https://gazebosim.org/docs/latest/ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs/"
">)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:318
msgid ""
"Ensure that the ROS CI build passes. Note that some builds have  warnings "
"which show up as failures on the Github UI while the build  actually "
"succeeded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:321
msgid ""
"For packages that are considered to be part of ROS core  (`gz_cmake_vendor`, "
"`gz_utils_vendor`, and `gz_math_vendor`), start  additional CI tests using "
"ci.ros2.org to build and test all ROS core  packages that depend on these "
"Gazebo vendor packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:325
msgid ""
"To do so, start a new [`ci_launcher`](https://ci.ros2.org/job/ci_launcher/) "
"build with the following parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:328
msgid ""
"`CI_BRANCH_TO_TEST`: branch name of the PR (e.g. `releasepy/rolling/3.1.1`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:329
msgid ""
"`CI_ROS2_REPOS_URL`: If the vendor package is going to `rolling`, this can "
"be skipped, otherwise use `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ros2/ros2/"
"$ROSDISTRO/ros2.repos` where `$ROSDISTRO` is replaced by the target ROS "
"distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:332
msgid ""
"`CI_UBUNTU_DISTRO`: Pick the Ubuntu distro that matches the target ROS "
"distribution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:333
msgid ""
"`CI_ROS_DISTRO`: The target ROS distribution. For Harmonic this is `jazzy`, "
"for Ionic this is `rolling` until `kilted` is released."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:334
msgid ""
"`CI_BUILD_ARGS`: `--event-handlers console_cohesion+ console_package_list+ --"
"cmake-args -DINSTALL_EXAMPLES=OFF -DSECURITY=ON -"
"DAPPEND_PROJECT_NAME_TO_INCLUDEDIR=ON  --packages-above-and-dependencies "
"$VENDOR_PACKAGE` where `$VENDOR_PACKAGE` is the name of the Gazebo vendor "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:335
msgid ""
"`CI_TEST_ARGS`: `--event-handlers console_cohesion+ --retest-until-pass 2 --"
"ctest-args -LE xfail --pytest-args -m 'not xfail' --executor sequential --"
"packages-above $VENDOR_PACKAGE` where `$VENDOR_PACKAGE` is the name of the "
"Gazebo vendor package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:337
msgid ""
"Note: you might have to ask the Infrastructure team to get permission to run "
"builds on ci.ros2.org."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:340
msgid "Once all of CI builds are successful, merge the PR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:341
msgid ""
"Make sure you have the required permission by checking  <https://github.com/"
"ros2-gbp/ros2-gbp-github-org/blob/latest/gazebo.tf>.  If your username is "
"not there, follow  [these instructions](https://docs.ros.org/en/rolling/How-"
"To-Guides/Releasing/Release-Team-Repository.html#join-a-release-team)  to "
"get added to the release team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:346
msgid ""
"Follow the steps of releasing a ROS package to release the vendor  package  "
"<https://docs.ros.org/en/rolling/How-To-Guides/Releasing/Subsequent-Releases."
"html>.  View the [versioning scheme](#versioning-scheme-for-gazebo-ros-"
"vendor-packages)  section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:352
msgid "Versioning scheme for Gazebo-ROS vendor packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:354
msgid ""
"The Gazebo vendor packages for ROS follow a specific versioning scheme to "
"ensure compatibility and proper ordering across different ROS distributions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:357
msgid ""
"**Patch version:** Bump the patch version if the package has already been "
"released for the target ROS distribution. This is almost always what you "
"want to do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:360
msgid "**Minor version:** Bump the minor version in the following cases:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:361
msgid ""
"If the package is being released into `rolling` and if the release happens "
"immediately after a new ROS distribution has been branched off of `rolling`. "
"The intention here is that all release branches (e.g. `jazzy`, `kilted`, "
"`rolling`, etc.) have distinct minor version numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:365
msgid ""
"When the underlying Gazebo package's major version number is bumped (e.g., "
"moving from `gz-math7` to `gz-math8`). This usually corresponds to a new "
"Gazebo collection release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:368
msgid "**Major version:** Never bump the major version number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:369
msgid ""
"**Bloom track:** When creating new branches for a vendor package (e.g. "
"branching off `rolling` for a newly released ROS distribution), ensure the "
"bloom track is updated accordingly. **It is critical to check that the "
"correct track is being used when making a release after a new ROS "
"distribution has been branched off of `rolling`.** There are two main cases:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:375
msgid ""
"**Core vendor packages (`gz_cmake_vendor`, `gz_utils_vendor`, and "
"`gz_math_vendor`):** These packages might be released into a new ROS "
"distribution automatically from the `rolling` branch. In this case, a new "
"stable branch should be created for the new ROS distribution, and the bloom "
"track should be updated to point to this new branch. It may be best to edit "
"the `tracks.yaml` file manually in the release repository to ensure that the "
"new track points to the correct branch while the `rolling` track continues "
"to point to the `rolling` branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:383
msgid ""
"**Non-core vendor packages:** For these packages, we are responsible for "
"branching off and making the release. The steps are: branch off from "
"`rolling`, then make the release using `bloom-release` with the `--edit-"
"track` flag to update the tracking information for the new distribution. The "
"`rolling` branch should continue to track the `rolling` distribution without "
"any changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releases-instructions.md:390
msgid ""
"Refer to the [bloom documentation](https://docs.ros.org/en/rolling/How-To-"
"Guides/Releasing/Release-Track.html) for more information."
msgstr ""
